// A move asks three parties, and each answers for itself: the thing
// (`depart`), the container it is leaving (`release`) and the one it is
// entering (`accept`). The world writes all three, as a kind and an
// object may. A guard only reads and decides; it ends in `allow`, in
// `refuse`, or by reaching its end, which allows.
world guards: sprout.World {
  visitors are Creature
  visitors arrive at hall

  depart (to) { refuse "The world goes nowhere." }
  release (item, to) {
    if (item.is(Creature)) { refuse "Nobody leaves the world." }
  }
  accept (item, from) { allow }
}
